Feature: Clone and transform Outbound FIA tables with DELETE_FLAG enforcement

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks" and schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the source tables are:
      | ods_free_drug           |
      | ods_non_contracting     |
      | ods_copay               |
    And the clone tables are:
      | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay_clone         |

  Scenario Outline: Drop clone tables if they exist
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" may exist
    When the process starts
    Then the clone table "<clone_table>" is dropped if it exists

    Examples:
      | clone_table                |
      | ods_free_drug_clone        |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone  |
      | ods_copay_clone            |

  Scenario Outline: Clone source table with DELETE_FLAG transformation and NOT NULL enforcement
    Given the source table "<source_table>" exists with column "Filler_1" (nullable)
    And the clone table "<clone_table>" does not exist
    When the table is cloned
    Then the clone table "<clone_table>" is created with schema:
      | <other_columns_before> | DELETE_FLAG (string, NOT NULL) | <other_columns_after> |
    And all other columns retain their names, types, and nullability
    And the column "Filler_1" is renamed to "DELETE_FLAG"
    And the "DELETE_FLAG" column is defined as NOT NULL in the DDL

    Examples:
      | source_table         | clone_table             | other_columns_before                | other_columns_after                |
      | ods_free_drug        | ods_free_drug_clone     | PM_ID, Shipment_Date, Dispense_ID   | Drug_Name, Quantity, Patient_ID    |
      | ods_non_contracting  | ods_non_contracting_clone | PM_ID, Shipment_Date, Dispense_ID | Facility, Units_Provided, Contract_Flag |
      | ods_copay            | ods_copay_clone         | PM_ID, NDC, Date_of_Service, Rx_Claim_Number | Copay_Amount, Plan_ID             |

  Scenario Outline: Filter out rows with NULL Filler_1 during clone
    Given the source table "<source_table>" contains rows with "Filler_1" values
      | Filler_1   |
      | "Y"        |
      | "N"        |
      | NULL       |
      | "DELETE"   |
    When the clone table "<clone_table>" is populated
    Then only rows where "Filler_1" is NOT NULL are included
    And the "DELETE_FLAG" column in "<clone_table>" contains only non-NULL values

    Examples:
      | source_table         | clone_table             |
      | ods_free_drug        | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting  | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay            | ods_copay_clone         |

  Scenario Outline: Validate NOT NULL constraint on DELETE_FLAG in clone table
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" is created
    When a row with NULL "DELETE_FLAG" is inserted
    Then the operation fails with error "NOT NULL constraint violated for DELETE_FLAG"

    Examples:
      | clone_table             |
      | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay_clone         |

  Scenario Outline: Validate schema consistency between source and clone tables
    Given the source table "<source_table>" and clone table "<clone_table>" exist
    When the clone table is created
    Then all columns except "Filler_1"/"DELETE_FLAG" have identical names, types, and nullability
    And the column order matches the source table, with "DELETE_FLAG" replacing "Filler_1"

    Examples:
      | source_table         | clone_table             |
      | ods_free_drug        | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting  | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay            | ods_copay_clone         |

  Scenario Outline: Error on type mismatch for DELETE_FLAG during clone
    Given the source table "<source_table>" has "Filler_1" values of type <actual_type>
    And the clone table "<clone_table>" expects "DELETE_FLAG" as string
    When a value of type <invalid_type> is encountered in "Filler_1"
    Then the operation fails with error "Type mismatch for DELETE_FLAG: expected string, got <invalid_type>"

    Examples:
      | source_table         | clone_table             | actual_type | invalid_type |
      | ods_free_drug        | ods_free_drug_clone     | string      | bigint       |
      | ods_non_contracting  | ods_non_contracting_clone | string    | boolean      |
      | ods_copay            | ods_copay_clone         | string      | double       |

  Scenario Outline: Error on duplicate primary key (if applicable)
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" has a unique constraint on <key_columns>
    When duplicate rows are inserted with same <key_columns> and different "DELETE_FLAG"
    Then the operation fails with error "Duplicate key violation on <key_columns>"

    Examples:
      | clone_table             | key_columns                        |
      | ods_free_drug_clone     | PM_ID, Dispense_ID                 |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone | PM_ID, Dispense_ID               |
      | ods_copay_clone         | PM_ID, Rx_Claim_Number             |

  Scenario Outline: Error on missing required columns during clone
    Given the source table "<source_table>" is missing required column "Filler_1"
    When the clone process is executed
    Then the operation fails with error "Source column Filler_1 not found in <source_table>"

    Examples:
      | source_table         |
      | ods_free_drug        |
      | ods_non_contracting  |
      | ods_copay            |

  Scenario Outline: Validate correct Unity Catalog and schema for clone tables
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" is created
    When the table is inspected
    Then the table exists in Unity Catalog "purgo_databricks" and schema "purgo_playground"

    Examples:
      | clone_table             |
      | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay_clone         |

  Scenario Outline: Validate data integrity after clone
    Given the clone table "<clone_table>" is populated
    When the data is queried
    Then all rows have non-NULL "DELETE_FLAG"
    And all other columns match the source data for those rows

    Examples:
      | clone_table             |
      | ods_free_drug_clone     |
      | ods_non_contracting_clone |
      | ods_copay_clone         |

# END
